Subject: win32u: fall back to a runtime MoltenVK soname when Wine is configured --without-vulkan
Origin: written for SSF Play (not from upstream).
Date-of-change: 2026-07-30
Files: dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
Change: dlls/win32u/vulkan.c references SONAME_LIBVULKAN unconditionally and fails to compile with --without-vulkan.
        Define a default ("libMoltenVK.dylib"); if the dlopen fails at run time Vulkan is simply unavailable.
        The distributed runtime does not ship MoltenVK, so Vulkan stays off.
License: LGPL-2.1-or-later, same as Wine.
---

--- a/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
@@ -2993,6 +2993,12 @@
     .p_map_instance_extensions = lazydrv_map_instance_extensions,
     .p_map_device_extensions = lazydrv_map_device_extensions,
 };
+
+/* built --without-vulkan: no compile-time soname; probe MoltenVK at runtime,
+ * dlopen failure below already degrades gracefully (vulkan just unavailable) */
+#ifndef SONAME_LIBVULKAN
+#define SONAME_LIBVULKAN "libMoltenVK.dylib"
+#endif
 
 static void vulkan_init_once(void)
 {
